{"title":"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">1998 CEMC Cayley #4</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">1998 CEMC Fermat #4</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Listing_Pairs)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Listing Pairs)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(General)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (General)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(answer_choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The product of two positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. What is the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/d/1fd9ef052fa397ecb4952c6f1d93bd5fa5a2baa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 52 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 101 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 29 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Listing_Pairs.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Listing_Pairs)\">Solution 1 (Listing Pairs)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Listing Pairs)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can list all of the factor pairs, and their sums and then see which is the largest:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b26c3cc0440936cde832dda0fe80184af5d409b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, 100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, which has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f33d4e24e0519a2b4a9522f1ea51d6345d5e8e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2, 50)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, which has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/1/5e1d1611143f5792dc0f61f3b130af88cb790c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$52$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/2/9f28db6fe2ecf10d048bf911aaf0531248698456.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4, 25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" />, which has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fb2bcf88c701b6cbd5fc7137012bb838b175fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5, 20)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />, which has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/7/177c0e170436248d2c7e92b813b58451a50f4c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10, 10)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, which has a sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>The rest of the pairs are just flipped, meaning that they'll just have the same sum as the previous ones. From the numbers listed, we see that the largest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110b4df315c9628ec2a119872a52824f7d40e38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28General.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(General)\">Solution 2 (General)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (General)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" /> would be obtained where one is the highest that it can be because the numbers would otherwise be closer together and would therefore have a smaller sum. This occurs when either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/8/9e89deaf87b4299ea61e482d3b8dd049b98e4269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/7/1272dd3806e9d5606535fd9a20d87ef1edfa52b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361ea4cb174e2c033a0a888475e35613e4aa3765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c8f3e00ae22fd486ff19143f21b84fc6933b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the largest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/8/6c80a7f939df1c4a9b18f15f98bc4f922b2989d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q = 1 + 100 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"222\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(answer_choices)\">Solution 3 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361ea4cb174e2c033a0a888475e35613e4aa3765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/c/26c8f3e00ae22fd486ff19143f21b84fc6933b0f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"17\" />, their sum would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />. The highest answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/110b4df315c9628ec2a119872a52824f7d40e38d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed {\\textbf {(B) } 101}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"75\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley\">1998 CEMC Cayley</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 5 (page does not exist)\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 7 (page does not exist)\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 8 (page does not exist)\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 9 (page does not exist)\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 12 (page does not exist)\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 13 (page does not exist)\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 14 (page does not exist)\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 15 (page does not exist)\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_16&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 16 (page does not exist)\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 17 (page does not exist)\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_18&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 18 (page does not exist)\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_CEMC_Cayley_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"1998 CEMC Cayley Problems/Problem 19 (page does not exist)\">19</a>